  "name": "Teacher as Researcher: Try, Reflect, Share",
  "type": "doc",
  "type_value": "module",
  "description": "Teacher-research is about curiosity—asking what’s happening with students and what it might mean.",
  "image": "public/aa7503e-MOdule 4.png",
  "html": "<h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-framing-our-work\">🖼️ Framing Our Work</h2><p>One goal of the <i>Literacy Th@t Works</i> professional learning experience is to recognize that teachers, like students, learn through inquiry. Teacher-research has a long history in education, grounded in the idea that teachers’ daily practice is a powerful source of knowledge. By paying attention to our classrooms, asking questions about what we notice, and trying small changes, teachers generate insights that not only support their own students but also contribute to the wider profession.</p><p>In this module, we take a step into teacher-research by choosing one strategy, trying it out, and paying close attention to how students respond. The goal is not perfection, but noticing—observing what happens, reflecting on what it might mean, and beginning to ask new questions. This process helps us learn from our own classrooms while also building habits of curiosity, reflection, and openness that will serve us in more in-depth inquiries to come.</p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-what-to-expect\">📝What to Expect</h2><p>You will notice that this module is a bit different from Modules 1-3. Instead of focusing on learning a new strategy, you’ll engage in a cycle of teacher-research: choosing a strategy from earlier modules, trying it out with your students, and reflecting on what you notice. To support this process, the module includes three discussions—one for preparing to teach, one for reflecting during teaching, and one for looking back afterward. You’ll participate in all three discussions to earn the discussion badge for this module.</p><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\" id=\"h_in-this-module-you-will\">In this module, you will:</h3><p>✅Step into the role of <b>teacher-researcher</b> by choosing one strategy from Modules 1–3 to focus on.</p><p>✅ Participate in a cycle of <b>three connected discussions</b>: preparing to teach, reflecting during teaching (including sharing artifacts), and reflecting after teaching.</p><p>✅ Share your observations, artifacts, and reflections with peers to notice patterns and learn together.</p><p>✅ <b>Earn the Teacher as Researacher microcredential</b> by connecting with your facilitator to reflect more deeply on what you learned, upload an artifact or anecdote, and identify next steps or new questions for your teaching.</p><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"7fe3efc9-3b1c-4bef-a183-5f69e1766d51\" data-doc-type=\"discussion\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/7fe3efc9-3b1c-4bef-a183-5f69e1766d51\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Discussion</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Preparing to Teach</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Share which strategy you’ve chosen to focus on and why you chose it.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/7f25d15-Doc%20Image%20Dimensions%20%2866%29.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"d4fbcb24-09a4-4ed7-9637-7dfa01bbb64c\" data-doc-type=\"discussion\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/d4fbcb24-09a4-4ed7-9637-7dfa01bbb64c\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Discussion</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">During Teaching</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Reflect on what you’re noticing in the moment and share an artifact that captures your students’ responses.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/86a121e-Doc%20Image%20Dimensions%20%2866%29.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"d3ecda66-200f-430c-bda4-45d4c826bc83\" data-doc-type=\"discussion\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/d3ecda66-200f-430c-bda4-45d4c826bc83\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Discussion</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">After Teaching</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Step back to consider what you’ve learned from trying the strategy and what new questions or next steps you see ahead.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/01dc7b9-Doc%20Image%20Dimensions%20%2866%29.png\"></div></a></div><p></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-earn-recognition\">🏅 Earn Recognition</h2><p><b>The Teacher as Researcher discussion badge is automatically awarded when you participate in all three Teacher as Research Discussions above.</b></p><div data-type=\"badge-embed\" data-badge-id=\"1b36800d-4c9b-430b-933e-ef553c6961d7\" data-badge-type=\"badge\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/badge/1b36800d-4c9b-430b-933e-ef553c6961d7\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Badge</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Teacher as Researcher Discussions</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This badge recognizes your participation in the three-part discussion cycle for this module. By posting and responding in each stage—before, during, and after teaching—you contribute to a shared inquiry process where teachers learn from one another’s experiences. Together, these conversations help build a supportive community of teacher-researchers.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/9ae696b-Module%201%20Community%20Cultivating%20Literacy.png\"></div></a></div><p><b>Click below to submit your learning reflection and earn your microcredential for this module.</b></p><div data-type=\"badge-embed\" data-badge-id=\"4d7461a3-2cff-4c86-9e7a-38cc46e34f45\" data-badge-type=\"micro_credential\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/badge/4d7461a3-2cff-4c86-9e7a-38cc46e34f45\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Micro Credential</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Teacher as Researcher: Cultivating Literacy Routines</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This microcredential recognizes your work as a teacher-researcher: choosing a strategy, trying it out with your students, and reflecting on what you learned from the process. By looking closely at student responses, sharing an artifact or anecdote, and considering implications for your teaching, you are taking the first steps toward ongoing inquiry in your classroom.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/dd10246-Module%204%20Teacher%20Cultivating%20Literacy.png\"></div></a></div><p></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-course-closure\">➡️ Course Closure</h2><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"10ef1ae5-5192-4016-9f56-3e9b2f8c6baa\" data-doc-type=\"page\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/10ef1ae5-5192-4016-9f56-3e9b2f8c6baa\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Page</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Fall Semester Closure</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Celebrate your completion of the course, confirm your credential, and share feedback to help us shape future learning experiences.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/42404f9-COurse%20Closure.png\"></div></a></div><p></p><p></p>",
